From bbf8f196561379c9ce38017f02e9729377999acd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:36:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 196/217] feat: a reflection ray that hits nothing shows the
 sky, not a second sun

A missed ray used to be handed a fake surface - albedo 1, F0 1, smoothness 1, a
normal of -rayDir at an arbitrary point MaxDistRay along the ray - and then run
through the whole forward lighting stack. That put a mirror-sharp GGX lobe at
F0 = 1 on top of an env probe that already contains the sun, i.e. a SECOND sun
in every reflected sky, plus specular sparks wherever a lamp sat near the ray.
Energy audit item 7 / E7, decision 09 section 9.1.

Now a miss runs no sun and no local-light loop at all (a new bDirectLights
parameter on Fwd_StandardOpaqueShading_Raytracing gates both), and an
above-horizon miss is resolved by the engine's own sky along the ray direction.

There is no sky render target to sample: CSkyStage::Execute runs SkyPassPS
straight into the HDR colour target from the sky-light manager's two lat-long
Nishita textures and, on a skybox level, from the level's skybox texture. So
ShadePass binds those three (t34/t35/t36, a wrap-U clamp-V linear sampler at s3)
and SVO_RT_SampleSky evaluates the same closed form Stars.cfx SkyPassPS does:
the Mie/Rayleigh phase-weighted dome, the night gradient, the skybox lerp and
the SkyDome_ScenePeakClamp ceiling. The sun disc needs no separate term - in
CE 5.7.1 the procedural sky has no sun sprite, what reads as the sun IS the Mie
phase function peaking at cosine 1, so the disc comes out with the same shape
and the same ceiling the direct view gets; on a skybox level it is painted in.

Exposure was checked against the pass rather than assumed: SetSkyParameters and
SetHDRSkyParameters multiply every radiance constant by GetSceneReferredExposure()
on the CPU and leave the textures unexposed, so the constants here are uploaded
the same way and the shader returns EXPOSED radiance - the units ShadePS's acc
is already in, whose single divide then cancels ApplyGI's multiply for a net x1,
the emissive rule of decision 06 section 6.4. Exactly 1.0 off the switch.

Below-horizon misses keep the env probe with the roughness mip, unchanged: a
lat-long dome says nothing below the horizon and what is down there is ground
the ray failed to reach inside e_svoTI_RT_MaxDistRay. With no sky bound at all
(interior level, sky stage inactive) SVO_SkyParams stays zero and every miss
keeps the probe. The SVO's analytic GetSkyColor is deliberately not the
fallback: it reads SvoParamsSkyColor and globalSpecCM, neither of which
ShadePass uploads or may bind.

Known gaps, documented in the shader: the moon, the stars and SkyPassPS's fog
blend are not carried. Cloud shadow is irrelevant to a sky lookup.

Sky.h gains two const accessors for the dome textures; nothing else outside
D3D_SVO.* and the SVO shaders is touched, and all of it is behind
e_svoTI_RT_Active.

